  :seon.task/plan "Owner: web (root's first item for web, 2026-11-16: Seon messaging, which tests2 coordinates through). DONE on jolt/web 25098d27af: a session's message is from its session's task agent (connection-agent), and an inbox by task reads every agent the task had.\nDONE on jolt/web 2bd3f09e66: a killed agent is ended (seon.task/agent-ended? reads its processes' ends; tests' client stuck on its killed agent). LATENT, not live (deps agrees, result/b218d79d): since by commit, as messages live only on main and every link's t is main's own.
OBSERVED 2026-11-16 15:58-16:00 (after root's restart), unexplained: a non-fresh attach of session/web was refused :seon.process/env-mismatch (tree da03279b, pins datahike and persistent-sorted-set) with no :unmerged in its answer, though its own merge of main had just written an unmerged [:datum 92955762703108944 :form/order] entry on :main/task-session-web (main-t 537013244, tx 537013245 at 08:58:27Z; result/d48db2c2, result/d8ead2a6), and root's program holds attach!'s :unmerged code (result/cdabb2ee). Not reproduced: the fresh attach after it moved the task to a new branch. Next time: read the refusal whole, and pm/unmerged on (:branch env) at that moment.
DONE: since by commit (an inbox reads new messages as main now minus main at the commit of since, a set difference, whatever a link's tx; the wait wakes on the same rule).
OPEN, in order: (1, done) since by commit (deps' finding: a message that reaches main by a merge is missed by a since that is a tx number): reproduce at the REPL first; read whether a merged :seon.message/to datom keeps its branch tx below since. (2) tests' report: after attach fresh=true answered new agent c2e37b48762968ca, every eval of client tests answered :seon.system/ended for old agent n281eb679a9b6642 (own-agent, my.root/held-agent), one eval reaching the new one first; a client's acts follow its session task's current agent, as its messages now do. (3) root: seon_agents shows each agent's :pid. (4) the inbox wait is on the task's current agent at the read: a fresh attach mid-wait wakes it only at its bound.\nPROOFS: red first at the agent, each named as it is written."
  :seon.task/kind :work
